# PATENT CLAIM

## Independent Claims

**Claim 1.** A computer-implemented method for thematically grouping and displaying raw data sets, the method comprising:

receiving, by one or more processors, a plurality of raw data sets from at least one data source;

extracting, from each raw data set of the plurality of raw data sets, a plurality of properties to generate a corresponding property vector, wherein each property vector comprises a plurality of numerical values representing characteristics of the corresponding raw data set;

assembling the property vectors into a property matrix, wherein each row or column of the property matrix corresponds to one property vector of the plurality of property vectors;

performing one or more matrix calculations on the property matrix to generate a similarity matrix, wherein the similarity matrix quantifies pairwise relationships between the plurality of raw data sets based on the extracted properties;

applying a dimensionality reduction algorithm to the similarity matrix to generate a reduced-dimension data set, wherein the reduced-dimension data set maps each raw data set of the plurality of raw data sets to a corresponding position within a three-dimensional coordinate space;

identifying, based on the reduced-dimension data set, one or more thematic clusters among the plurality of raw data sets, wherein raw data sets within a given thematic cluster share a threshold degree of similarity as determined by their respective positions within the three-dimensional coordinate space; and

generating, on a display device, a three-dimensional visualization representing the plurality of raw data sets, wherein the three-dimensional visualization depicts each raw data set as a graphical object positioned according to the reduced-dimension data set, and wherein raw data sets belonging to a common thematic cluster are visually distinguished from raw data sets belonging to a different thematic cluster.

---

**Claim 2.** A system for thematically grouping and displaying raw data sets, the system comprising:

one or more processors;

a display device communicatively coupled to the one or more processors; and

a non-transitory computer-readable medium storing instructions that, when executed by the one or more processors, cause the system to:

receive a plurality of raw data sets from at least one data source;

extract, from each raw data set of the plurality of raw data sets, a plurality of properties to generate a corresponding property vector;

construct a property matrix from the property vectors corresponding to the plurality of raw data sets;

compute, via one or more matrix operations performed on the property matrix, a similarity matrix representing pairwise similarity values among the plurality of raw data sets;

reduce a dimensionality of the similarity matrix using a dimensionality reduction technique to produce three-dimensional coordinate values for each raw data set of the plurality of raw data sets;

determine one or more thematic groupings among the plurality of raw data sets based on proximity of the three-dimensional coordinate values; and

render, on the display device, a three-dimensional visual representation of the plurality of raw data sets, wherein each raw data set is displayed as a graphical element at a position corresponding to its three-dimensional coordinate values, and wherein graphical elements corresponding to raw data sets within a same thematic grouping share a common visual attribute distinguishing them from graphical elements corresponding to raw data sets within a different thematic grouping.

---

**Claim 3.** A non-transitory computer-readable storage medium storing instructions that, when executed by one or more processors, cause the one or more processors to perform operations comprising:

receiving a plurality of raw data sets;

generating a property vector for each raw data set of the plurality of raw data sets by extracting a plurality of quantifiable properties therefrom;

organizing the property vectors into a property matrix;

performing a matrix transformation on the property matrix to derive a distance matrix or a similarity matrix representative of relationships among the plurality of raw data sets;

applying a dimensionality reduction algorithm to the distance matrix or the similarity matrix to generate a set of three-dimensional coordinates corresponding to the plurality of raw data sets;

clustering the plurality of raw data sets into one or more thematic groups based on the set of three-dimensional coordinates; and

causing display of a three-dimensional graphical representation in which each raw data set of the plurality of raw data sets is rendered as a discrete visual marker positioned according to the set of three-dimensional coordinates, the discrete visual marker being color-coded, shape-coded, or otherwise visually coded according to its corresponding thematic group.

---

## Dependent Claims

**Claim 4.** The method of claim 1, wherein extracting the plurality of properties comprises applying a natural language processing algorithm to textual content within the raw data sets to derive semantic features.

**Claim 5.** The method of claim 1, wherein performing the one or more matrix calculations comprises computing a cosine similarity, a Euclidean distance, or a Pearson correlation coefficient between pairs of property vectors.

**Claim 6.** The method of claim 1, wherein the dimensionality reduction algorithm comprises at least one of: principal component analysis (PCA), t-distributed stochastic neighbor embedding (t-SNE), uniform manifold approximation and projection (UMAP), or multidimensional scaling (MDS).

**Claim 7.** The method of claim 1, wherein identifying the one or more thematic clusters comprises applying a clustering algorithm selected from the group consisting of: k-means clustering, hierarchical clustering, DBSCAN, and Gaussian mixture modeling.

**Claim 8.** The method of claim 1, further comprising receiving, via an input device, a user interaction with a graphical object within the three-dimensional visualization, and in response, displaying additional information associated with the raw data set corresponding to the graphical object.

**Claim 9.** The method of claim 1, further comprising dynamically updating the three-dimensional visualization in response to receiving an additional raw data set, wherein updating comprises re-computing the property matrix, the similarity matrix, and the reduced-dimension data set to incorporate the additional raw data set.

**Claim 10.** The method of claim 1, wherein the three-dimensional visualization is navigable via user input to enable rotation, zooming, and panning within the three-dimensional coordinate space.

**Claim 11.** The method of claim 1, wherein each thematic cluster is rendered with a distinct color, and wherein the visual distinguishing further comprises rendering a boundary or enclosure encompassing the graphical objects belonging to a common thematic cluster.

**Claim 12.** The method of claim 1, wherein the plurality of properties comprises at least one of: metadata attributes, statistical measures, term frequency values, keyword occurrences, or categorical labels associated with the raw data sets.

**Claim 13.** The system of claim 2, wherein the instructions further cause the system to normalize the property vectors prior to constructing the property matrix.

**Claim 14.** The system of claim 2, wherein the one or more matrix operations comprise a singular value decomposition (SVD) of the property matrix.

**Claim 15.** The non-transitory computer-readable storage medium of claim 3, wherein the operations further comprise assigning a label to each thematic group based on shared properties among the raw data sets within the thematic group, and displaying the label proximate to the discrete visual markers corresponding to the thematic group within the three-dimensional graphical representation.

# Independent Method Claim

**Claim 1.** A computer-implemented method for visualizing multi-dimensional data, the method comprising:

receiving, by one or more processors, a dataset comprising a plurality of data records, each data record comprising a plurality of feature values and an associated auxiliary attribute, wherein the auxiliary attribute comprises at least one of a timestamp value or a unique identifier value;

applying, by the one or more processors, a clustering or classification algorithm to the plurality of feature values of the dataset to assign each data record of the plurality of data records to one of a plurality of clusters or classes;

applying, by the one or more processors, a dimensionality reduction algorithm to the plurality of feature values of the dataset to generate, for each data record, a corresponding pair of reduced-dimension coordinate values representing the data record in a two-dimensional coordinate space, wherein the dimensionality reduction algorithm is applied independently of the auxiliary attribute;

generating, by the one or more processors, a three-dimensional coordinate for each data record by combining the corresponding pair of reduced-dimension coordinate values with a third coordinate value derived from the auxiliary attribute associated with the data record, wherein the third coordinate value is assigned along an axis orthogonal to the two-dimensional coordinate space;

associating, by the one or more processors, a visual indicator with each data record based on the cluster or class to which the data record was assigned; and

rendering, on a display device, a three-dimensional visualization comprising a graphical representation of each data record positioned according to its respective three-dimensional coordinate and displayed with its associated visual indicator, wherein the three-dimensional visualization is interactively navigable to permit rotation, zoom, or filtering of the graphical representations relative to the axis corresponding to the auxiliary attribute.

---

Would you like me to also draft:
1. Dependent claims (e.g., specifying clustering algorithm types like k-means/DBSCAN, dimensionality reduction methods like t-SNE/UMAP/PCA, and interactive filtering features)?
2. A parallel **system claim** and **CRM (computer-readable medium) claim** to round out the independent claim set?
3. Alternative claim language emphasizing the "auxiliary attribute as third axis" as a novel technical solution (useful for the specification's technical problem/solution narrative)?

# Patent Claim

**Claim 1.** A computer-implemented method for visualizing grouped data, the method comprising:

receiving, by a processor, a plurality of data records, each data record associated with a group identifier and a plurality of properties;

generating, for each of the plurality of data records, a property vector representing values corresponding to the plurality of properties associated with the data record;

forming a data matrix by aggregating the property vectors generated for the plurality of data records, wherein rows of the data matrix correspond to the plurality of data records and columns of the data matrix correspond to the plurality of properties;

computing, by the processor, at least one of (i) one or more clusters of the data matrix by applying a clustering algorithm to the property vectors to group the plurality of data records into a plurality of clusters based on similarity of the values of the plurality of properties, or (ii) one or more summarizations of the data matrix by applying a summarization algorithm to the property vectors to generate aggregated representations of the plurality of data records;

reducing dimensionality of the data matrix, or of the one or more clusters or the one or more summarizations computed therefrom, from an original dimensionality to a two-dimensional representation by applying a dimensionality reduction algorithm, thereby generating a plurality of two-dimensional coordinate pairs each corresponding to a data record, a cluster, or a summarization;

identifying a third-dimension value for each of the plurality of two-dimensional coordinate pairs, wherein the third-dimension value corresponds to at least one of a timestamp associated with the corresponding data record or a group identifier associated with the corresponding data record;

expanding each of the plurality of two-dimensional coordinate pairs into a corresponding three-dimensional coordinate by combining the two-dimensional coordinate pair with the identified third-dimension value, thereby generating a plurality of three-dimensional coordinates; and

rendering, on a display device, a three-dimensional visualization of the plurality of data records based on the plurality of three-dimensional coordinates, wherein the three-dimensional visualization depicts relationships among the plurality of data records across the third dimension.

---

**Claim 2 (dependent).** The method of claim 1, wherein the clustering algorithm comprises at least one of a k-means clustering algorithm, a hierarchical clustering algorithm, or a density-based clustering algorithm.

**Claim 3 (dependent).** The method of claim 1, wherein the dimensionality reduction algorithm comprises at least one of principal component analysis (PCA), t-distributed stochastic neighbor embedding (t-SNE), or uniform manifold approximation and projection (UMAP).

**Claim 4 (dependent).** The method of claim 1, wherein the third-dimension value corresponds to the timestamp, and wherein the rendering step comprises generating an animated or temporally-ordered visualization depicting changes in the plurality of data records over time.

**Claim 5 (dependent).** The method of claim 1, wherein the third-dimension value corresponds to the group identifier, and wherein the rendering step comprises spatially separating the plurality of three-dimensional coordinates according to the group identifier along the third dimension.

**Claim 6 (dependent).** The method of claim 1, further comprising receiving, via a user interface, a selection of the third-dimension value from among a plurality of candidate third-dimension values including at least a time-based value and an identifier-based value.

